    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 4th with a heavy emphasis on exploiting favorable matchups against struggling arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** headlines our offensive output with a stellar 82.12 score; his assumed #2 spot against J.T. Ginn provides the ideal runway for his elite sprint speed to impact the scarcest category, SB, while benefiting from a +5% wind-out factor. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (77.93) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.21) are in prime positions to capitalize on Lucas Giolito\u2019s poor 6.49 xERA. The decision to stack **Kyle Schwarber** at leadoff is aggressive, but his 0.389 xwOBA suggests he is the primary engine for our HR and RBI production tonight. **Christian Yelich** rounds out our elite tier at 74.33, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Houser creates a high-floor outcome for our Roto averages.\n\nWhile the core is set, the bench remains a point of contention. **Caleb Durbin** just narrowly edged out our utility options, securing a 60.30 score due to favorable park factors and steady usage. We are monitoring the status of **Pedro Ramirez**, **Jose Fernandez**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Yordan Alvarez**, all of whom are currently tagged with \"Lineup Pending.\" Should **Pedro Ramirez** or **Jose Fernandez** slide down further in the order than our assumed #8 spots, we may see their scores dip into the sub-40 range, forcing a pivot toward our bench depth. Our minor league prospects like **Hyeseong Kim** and **Zac Veen** remain sidelined, and with **Junior Caminero** and **Colt Keith** suffering from an organizational off-day, our flexibility is limited. We must also exercise caution with **Kazuma Okamoto** (46.82); while his platoon advantage is positive, he faces the toughest arm of the night in Chris Sale, making him a marginal play despite his talent.",
